1. Executive Summary
HACA currently operates the SHO App — an internal staff management platform used by administrators, school heads, mentors, and academic leads to manage student batches, attendance, module exams, assignments, and class planning across multiple schools.
The HACA LMS is a student-facing Learning Management System that integrates tightly with the existing SHO App. It allows students to access course content, submit assignments, take quizzes, track their progress, and view attendance and exam results — all driven by data already managed in the SHO App.
Both systems share a common MongoDB database and JWT authentication layer, making data sync seamless without a separate API bridge. This significantly reduces build complexity and ongoing infrastructure cost.

2. LMS Scope
What the LMS is:
Gives each student a personal login and dashboard
Shows enrolled courses mapped from SHO App batches
Delivers course content — video, PDF, text, external links
Lets students take quizzes and submit assignments
Displays attendance and exam results pulled from SHO App data
Tracks progress through each course with visual indicators
Issues certificates with unique IDs and QR codes on completion
What the LMS is NOT:
Does not replace the SHO App for staff operations
Does not manage schools, batches, or user roles (stays in SHO App)
Does not mark attendance (SHO staff continue to do that)
Mentors and admins continue using SHO App — LMS is purely student-facing

