9. Security Considerations
Area
Implementation
Role isolation
Student JWT cannot access any SHO App admin endpoints. Enforced at middleware level.
File uploads
File type whitelist (PDF, DOCX, ZIP, images only). Virus scanning on storage.
Quiz integrity
Questions and answers never sent to client before submission. Option order randomised.
Rate limiting
Login attempts limited. Quiz submission rate-limited to prevent brute force.
Certificate fraud
Unique IDs stored in DB. Public verification at /verify/{certificateId}.
Data privacy
Students can only access their own data. No cross-student data leakage possible.


10. Open Questions for Decision
These must be resolved before or during Phase 1:
Q1 — Video hosting strategy? YouTube embeds = ₹0 bandwidth, fastest to launch. Self-hosted on R2 = ~₹1,000 more/month but full brand control. Recommendation: start with YouTube, migrate if branding becomes a priority.
Q2 — Multi-course per student? Current SHO App is one batch per student. If multi-batch is needed, Course and Progress data models change significantly. Must decide before Phase 1 starts.
Q3 — Offline support? PWA setup for video/PDF downloads. Nice-to-have, not MVP. Defer to post-launch.
Q4 — Live class tool? Google Meet links = 1-day work. Zoom API = 1–2 weeks. Recommend Meet links for Phase 1.
Q5 — Existing student migration? Bulk account creation script needed for ~1,000 existing students. Estimate 1–2 days of work. Required before launch.
Q6 — Certificate design? Who designs the template? Needs brand approval from leadership. Must be resolved by end of Phase 3.
Q7 — Domain? learn.haca.ac (custom, ~₹1,100/year) vs learn.hacashoapp.vercel.app (free). Custom domain strongly recommended for student credibility.
Q8 — Mentor LMS read view? Should mentors see a read-only LMS view, or does the SHO App analytics panel cover their needs? Affects Phase 5 scope.

